3.168

### New Features
- [API] Public API for other addons: the tracking core is now consumable at runtime via `ActionDurationReminder.load("Core")` — query actions by ability id/name/hotbar slot, access the live action maps, and hook the ~100ms update tick via the `Core:update` extension key; `ActionDurationReminder.apiVersion` (major version, currently 3) gates compatibility — documented APIs stay stable within one apiVersion. Full reference: `docs/API.md` on GitHub and `API.md` inside the release zip.
- [API] Embedded core distribution: the release zip now ships an `embedded/` folder with guarded, UI-less core sources plus `EMBED.md`, so other addons can embed the ADR core behind `## OptionalDependsOn: ActionDurationReminder` — when standalone ADR is installed it always takes precedence; otherwise the embedded copy activates and exposes the identical API. The embedded copy stores its settings under a host-specific saved-variables name (e.g. `YourAddonADRSV`, passed as the 2nd argument of `ADR_EMBED.activate`), so it never shares `ADRSV` with the standalone addon.
- Added an Alert "Text Color" setting: the popup alert's text color is now customizable via a color picker (Settings -> Alert), matching the existing bar color options.
- [API] Added `action:getEffectList()` as the supported accessor for the effects currently matched to an action.

3.167

### Bug Fixes
- Shift bar layering vs the native ability bar frame now matches keyboard mode in gamepad mode: the gamepad slot frame is a plain "Backdrop" child control that the shift bar texture (created later at the same draw layer/level) used to cover; in gamepad mode the shift bar is re-parented under the slot's Button control (the first slot child, which renders no state texture in gamepad mode) so it draws below the native frame. Re-applied automatically when switching between keyboard and gamepad UI.

3.166

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed recasting Channeled Focus / Restoring Focus not refreshing the slot timer: two causes fixed — (1) the re-cast's GAINED_DURATION combat event only carries the player buff's ability id, which no longer matches the ground rune stack effect's stamped combatEventId, so the inherited stack effect kept the old endTime; the ground/area re-cast branch now also pulls a stale same-family stack effect forward to the new duration. (2) combat-event queue loops iterate every matching action in the action queue, including the superseded old one, whose re-save stole idActionMap back from the fresh action; saveAction now refuses to re-register superseded actions.

3.165

### New Features
- Debug logs now go to an in-game console (/adrlog) instead of the chat frame; use it to filter and copy logs when reporting issues. Chat output can be re-enabled in settings if preferred.

3.164

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed the "Move Shift Bar" frame teleporting off screen after being dragged (U51 regression): the engine now computes drag offsets in absolute screen space for controls anchored to non-GuiRoot controls, so the positioning frame is anchored to GuiRoot with offsets converted from slot3's live position; offsets are also no longer saved while slot3 reports an invalid position.

3.163

### New Features
- Nothing Wasted (Necromancer) tracking: the hidden stacking buff is now displayed on the Shocking Siphon (and its morphs) slot with the current stack count and a 12s window countdown; stack decay refreshes the window, and the display bootstraps after login/zone changes with stacks already running.

3.162

### New Features
- Unified stack effect management: stack effects, whether gradually accumulated (e.g. Grim Focus) or granted at once, now share a single stack slot; the second stack slot is reserved for future special-case logic.
- Crystal Weapon support: stacks granted 3 at once and consumed one by one by empowered attacks now display 3 → 2 → 1 with the 6s buff timer, and the slot clears when the stacks are exhausted or expire.
- "Log tracked effects in chat" now covers all paths an effect can enter an action (effect events, combat events, buff polling), letting players discover ability ids for the core blacklist.

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed Crystal Weapon losing its stack count when re-casting while buffed: the replacement fade of the old buff instance (via combat event or effect events) no longer purges the freshly granted stack, and its expiry is carried over and refreshed by the follow-up duration event.
- Fixed Barbed Trap's '@' activation marker no longer showing after the official arm-time reduction from 2.5s to 1.5s: the activation delay is now measured from the original trap placement time rather than the reset action start.
- Crystal Weapon's 5s armor reduction debuff on targets is now classified as a tail effect displayed in low-priority brackets instead of role-preferred, and the now-redundant '>' marker was removed.
- The '@' activation marker now requires the activated effect's duration to strictly match the action's duration.

3.161

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed Aspect of Terror's useful debuff being discarded by the "Ignore Mismatched Debuff Durations" option when it lasted longer than the skill's own duration: its icon is now excluded from the filter, same as the existing Rune of Edric Horror exclusion.

3.160

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed Fire Keeper (and similar skills that apply a permanent tracker buff alongside a timed AoE) leaving a stale `stack=1` and a frozen timer after all timed effects expire: the permanent stack effect now goes stale when no timed effects remain in the action's effect list.
- Major/minor buffs that share the action's duration but arrive (or keep refreshing) well after the action started — e.g. Minor Fortitude / Minor Heroism while standing in a Fire Keeper AoE — are now demoted to low-priority display instead of being treated as a same-source main effect.

3.159

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed Carve (and other multi-target stacking DoTs) losing the boss's stack count and timer when adds spawn: the action now preserves the higher-stack instance (e.g. the boss's 3-stack / 32s long bleed) instead of letting a fresh 1-stack / 12s bleed from an add overwrite both the stack count and the displayed timer.

3.158a

### Improvements
- When an action's main effect (icon-matching) is purged and only minor buff effects remain, those minor buffs are demoted to low priority, and a red "0" is displayed on the stack label to indicate the main effect is gone. For example, Arcanist's Runic Defense grants a heal-on-low-HP effect along with minor buffs — when the heal triggers and the main effect fades, the red "0" reminds you to recast even though minor buffs still have time left.

3.157

### Improvements
- Added reserved words so they won't be treated as a short word in ability name matching.
- Off Balance debuff now matches non-strictly, improving effect tracking for abilities that apply this debuff.

3.156

### New Features
- Added progress bar direction option: horizontal (left-fixed, shrinks right to left) or vertical (bottom-fixed, shrinks top to bottom).

3.155

### Bug Fixes
- Chat Alert is now disabled by default for new users. The welcome dialog can be dismissed without enabling.
- Chat Alert enabled/disabled setting is now account-wide (applies to all characters).

3.154

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed Chat Alert welcome prompt showing on every character. The prompt is now properly account-wide.

3.153

### Improvements
- Added Chinese ability name patch to fix ESO translation typos for correct ability matching.

3.152

### New Features
- Added progress bar display mode for action bar timers: a horizontal bar that shrinks from right to left, independently configurable with custom color and opacity.

### Improvements
- Chat Alert now uses game's chat color settings from Settings > Social > Chat Colors.
- Added guild prefix format options for guild channel messages: [Guild Name], [<Index>], or [<Index>-<Guild Name>].
- Added alignment option for Chat Alert messages: Left, Center, or Right.

3.151

### New Features
- Added Chat Alert module: displays group chat messages as popup alerts during combat, ensuring important callouts are never missed.

3.150

### New Features
- Added LEVEL_MAJOR_MINOR_BUFF priority level: major/minor buff effects are now deprioritized when they don't match the skill's own duration, preventing them from overriding the primary effect timer.

### Improvements
- Synced all i18n translation files with current code keys, removing 65 obsolete entries and adding 51 new entries.

3.149

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed UI error caused by missing models reference in stack label display.

### Refactoring
- Moved stackEffect validity check into getStackEffect/getStackEffect2 getters, eliminating the need for callers to check expiry themselves.

3.148

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed stack effect timer flickering at 0.0 when FADED event is not received.

3.147

### Improvements
- Fade event now checks stackEffect as fallback for stackCount2 mismatch, and supports hitValue increment detection alongside descriptionNum matching.

3.146

### Improvements
- Changed "Clear on Combat End" option to only clear area/ground actions instead of all actions.

3.145

### Improvements
- Action icon now updates after skill usage to match the current action bar icon.

3.144c

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed Lua error "function expected instead of nil" in Alert.lua when action is renewed during combat.

3.144

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed alert showing wrong ability icon after bar swap for non-crafted abilities (e.g., Budding Seeds).

3.143

### New Features
- Added Power Lash Guide feature for Dragonknight, showing a prompt icon when Power Lash is ready.
- Added popup alerts for Arcanist's Crux stacks.
- Added configurable color for low priority effect labels.
- Added blinking effect for stackLabel when stageInfoBlink is set.

### Improvements
- Refactored alert system to rule-based architecture with independent trigger marks.
- Implemented global crux sharing across multiple Arcanist actions.
- Refactored stackCount to read from stackEffect as single source of truth.
- Added duration source tracking to distinguish tick/channel/filter/priority effect durations.
- Improved positioning frame UI with ESO-style borders.
- Refactored debug logging system with three-tier marking scheme and ability name filtering.
- Created standalone Debug.lua module with fine-grained debug control.

### Performance
- Cached action and effect matching for improved performance.

### Refactor
- Moved action leak detection from Alert to Core module.

### Bug Fixes
- Fixed ShiftBar sizing to work correctly in Gamepad mode by using dynamic slot dimensions instead of hardcoded 50px.

